1
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:20,120
De vez em quando, eu me lembro daquela luta de espadas.

2
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:23,430
Naquele dia,

3
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:26,740
eu perdi a minha resposta e, ao mesmo tempo, a encontrei.

4
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:30,680
Mas nem uma única coisa mudou.

5
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:35,300
Ele continua sendo ele, e eu continuo sendo eu.

6
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,440
Apenas as memórias se desvanecem.

7
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:42,780
Nenhum de nós acreditava que algo mudaria como resultado daquela batalha.

8
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:47,950
Dois anos se passaram

9
00:00:48,830 --> 00:00:51,110
desde que enfrentei o meu próprio ideal.

10
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:53,710
Não vou receber uma resposta pronta,

11
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:56,490
for a long, long time yet.

12
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:15,600
Thanks for always being so considerate.

13
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:20,350
But I've told you a million times that I can manage without breakfast.

14
00:01:21,110 --> 00:01:23,080
I can't have that.

15
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:24,840
You're allowing me to live here,

16
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:27,130
so it's the least I can do as your attendant.

17
00:01:28,790 --> 00:01:32,210
You're still not a morning person, huh?

18
00:01:32,210 --> 00:01:34,120
That's surprising.

19
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:37,750
Having at least one little quirk like that

20
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:40,120
gives a girl some charm, right?

21
00:01:54,110 --> 00:01:55,520
Schedule-wise,

22
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:58,920
I have a special lecture on cutting in mineralogy today.

23
00:01:58,920 --> 00:01:59,900
How about you?

24
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:03,100
I think I just have core subjects all morning.

25
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:05,380
Then we're together half the day.

26
00:02:05,380 --> 00:02:07,280
Let's meet at our usual spot this afternoon.

27
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,160
Tohsaka...

28
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:15,740
Actually, never mind.

29
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,710
What's the matter?

30
00:02:28,710 --> 00:02:30,300
Do you know that person?

31
00:02:30,710 --> 00:02:34,060
No, we've just walked by each other a few times.

32
00:02:35,290 --> 00:02:36,560
I was just thinking...

33
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:40,270
This is a bit belated, but it just hit me how strange this is.

34
00:02:40,270 --> 00:02:44,660
Why is an outsider like me being allowed to study magic at a place like this?

35
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:46,570
For the last time, you aren't an outsider.

36
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:49,070
I told you Clock Tower's rules, remember?

37
00:02:49,430 --> 00:02:51,840
When you're a noted mage's rightful heir,

38
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:54,330
you're always at risk of having others try to kill you.

39
00:02:54,940 --> 00:03:01,960
Given that, a mage has the right to be accompanied by a follower or pupil for their protection.

40
00:03:02,330 --> 00:03:05,570
You're enrolled here as my follower,

41
00:03:05,570 --> 00:03:07,590
so hold your head up high.

42
00:03:07,590 --> 00:03:11,220
I know that. I'm grateful to you, Tohsaka.

43
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:14,960
You ought to be. Getting you in wasn't easy.

44
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,850
Well, it's only a three-year special exemption.

45
00:03:18,330 --> 00:03:20,100
But be careful.

46
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:23,330
As a school, this place has rules,

47
00:03:23,330 --> 00:03:25,730
but none of the normal social laws.

48
00:03:25,730 --> 00:03:28,790
It may only be considered a "minor ritual in the Far East,"

49
00:03:28,790 --> 00:03:33,370
but you're a mage who survived the Holy Grail War.

50
00:03:33,370 --> 00:03:36,090
Some here won't take kindly to that,

51
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:37,370
so if you let down your guard...

52
00:03:37,370 --> 00:03:38,620
Your guard is down!

53
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:40,510
Guess again!

54
00:03:46,630 --> 00:03:48,380
Sherou!

55
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:50,280
Luvia-san?

56
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:52,350
Don't be so impersonal!

57
00:03:52,350 --> 00:03:55,390
You're not currently on the clock as her butler, right?

58
00:03:55,390 --> 00:03:59,350
"Miss Luvia" is perfectly fine, Sherou!

59
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:03,580
Don't get so chummy with him!

60
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:05,850
Oh, Miss Tohsaka...

61
00:04:05,850 --> 00:04:10,400
Not only are we classmates, we're also neighbors living in the same apartment building.

62
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:13,680
What's so inappropriate about this?

63
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:15,510
Everything about it is inappropriate!

64
00:04:15,510 --> 00:04:17,030
Relax, Tohsaka.

65
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:20,890
Let's try to get along with our classmates, okay?

66
00:04:20,890 --> 00:04:25,670
Anyway, we only got the third floor of 
that building thanks to Luvia-san, right?

67
00:04:25,670 --> 00:04:27,690
Sherou!

68
00:04:27,690 --> 00:04:28,630
Hey!

69
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,570
Don't let it go to your head!

70
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:37,050
Oh, dear! O-Oh, oh, oh, oh!

71
00:04:37,530 --> 00:04:39,170
Change in plans!

72
00:04:39,170 --> 00:04:40,680
Our next class will be...

73
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:47,130
Self-defense.

74
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:50,570
The class where one expresses one's vitality 
through physical ability.

75
00:04:50,950 --> 00:04:53,190
The Edelfelt family's designated heir,

76
00:04:53,190 --> 00:04:55,160
Luviagelita Edelfelt,

77
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,570
will provide you with a much-needed lesson.

78
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,520
Excellent!

79
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,540
You might be mistaken for a gorilla! Miss Gorilla!

80
00:05:24,540 --> 00:05:26,390
That's right, keep talking!

81
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:31,020
It hurts! It hurts so bad!

82
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,780
What's the deal with that new-money bitch?

83
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:38,900
I nailed her right in the medulla oblongata, so why wouldn't she go down?!

84
00:05:42,150 --> 00:05:44,910
Luvia-san isn't a bad person, so just—

85
00:05:44,910 --> 00:05:47,080
Where did you two meet, anyway?!

86
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:51,840
Well, not long after we moved here, we both got lost...

87
00:05:56,110 --> 00:05:57,590
Ow, ow, ow! Ow!

88
00:05:59,770 --> 00:06:01,220
Oh, well.

89
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:03,480
I'll settle things with her eventually.

90
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:08,600
So, what will you do?

91
00:06:09,290 --> 00:06:13,100
You got an invitation, right? 
To officially join the Mages' Association?

92
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:15,610
Yeah.

93
00:06:16,330 --> 00:06:21,840
A mage's innate talents are evaluated and recorded, 
along with the nature of their soul.

94
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:24,620
They then become a mage affiliated with Clock Tower.

95
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:26,750
Isn't that a good thing?

96
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:32,000
Your activities would be restricted in some ways 
because you'd basically be indebted to the Association.

97
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:36,140
But it comes with a lot of perks for a mage,

98
00:06:36,140 --> 00:06:38,010
so most people would jump at it.

99
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:40,760
Yeah.

100
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:42,570
I guess you're right.

101
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:55,870
Becoming a Clock Tower member and a genuine mage...

102
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,780
It's the right decision.

103
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:02,160
But my beliefs lie elsewhere.

104
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:18,010
Tohsaka?

105
00:07:20,510 --> 00:07:24,350
Sorry, I overslept. I'll start breakfast right now.

106
00:07:24,350 --> 00:07:25,260
Emiya-kun...

107
00:07:27,430 --> 00:07:29,870
Will you go somewhere with me today?

108
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:56,090
What is this place?

109
00:07:56,090 --> 00:07:57,760
Glastonbury.

110
00:07:57,760 --> 00:08:00,170
A certain king's grave.

111
00:08:00,170 --> 00:08:05,080
You said you regretted not getting the chance to say a proper goodbye that day.

112
00:08:06,510 --> 00:08:09,300
I'll give you two some time alone.

113
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:22,760
I forgot that you were a king, Saber.

114
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:27,000
Thank you.

115
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:30,090
For what it's worth, I've come a long way since then.

116
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:37,080
This sure is a nice place.

117
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,770
Yeah, it is.

118
00:08:38,770 --> 00:08:46,220
It feels weird to think that, in a place like this, people once led lives nothing like ours.

119
00:08:46,710 --> 00:08:49,460
Like they say, it's a big old world.

120
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:52,190
It's already been six months since we came to England.

121
00:08:52,190 --> 00:08:54,880
For me, every day is one surprise after another.

122
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:56,100
How about you?

123
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:58,420
Same here.

124
00:08:58,420 --> 00:09:01,060
I've learned how insignificant I am.

125
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:04,250
I became a Master, fought alongside Saber,

126
00:09:04,250 --> 00:09:06,610
and survived the Holy Grail War, right?

127
00:09:06,610 --> 00:09:10,040
I thought I could do anything if I put my mind to it.

128
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:14,200
But by the very next day, that arrogance had faded away.

129
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,800
I'm not surprised.

130
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:18,880
You never change, Shirou.

131
00:09:19,310 --> 00:09:21,440
I understand now.

132
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:25,030
The Holy Grail War was a major event.

133
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:27,170
But now that I've seen a bit more of the world,

134
00:09:27,170 --> 00:09:29,390
it's clear that it was only one event of many.

135
00:09:29,390 --> 00:09:32,090
Still, it left a significant mark

136
00:09:32,090 --> 00:09:33,800
and sowed the seeds of change.

137
00:09:34,710 --> 00:09:37,340
I might not have personally matured,

138
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:41,990
but I just saw for myself how special that battle was.

139
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:45,600
I'm the opposite.

140
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:49,410
I'm starting to believe it wasn't anything special at all.

141
00:09:49,950 --> 00:09:54,140
The Holy Grail War, Clock Tower, simple days like this...

142
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:56,390
They'll never fundamentally change.

143
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:59,070
You relied on Saber,

144
00:09:59,070 --> 00:10:03,920
but in her life, Saber herself relied on the people of the past.

145
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:06,390
We're all connected.

146
00:10:06,390 --> 00:10:08,410
I think we walk through life 
not only on our own feet,

147
00:10:08,410 --> 00:10:12,030
but also by standing on the shoulders 
of those who came before.

148
00:10:12,650 --> 00:10:16,800
Clock Tower is steeped in ancient traditions.

149
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:20,940
So every day, while I'm studying, 
I feel like someone is judging me.

150
00:10:21,510 --> 00:10:25,440
Like they're asking what my contribution will be.

151
00:10:25,990 --> 00:10:27,290
Oh, I get it.

152
00:10:28,250 --> 00:10:30,570
It was that simple, huh?

153
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:48,050
Hey! Wake up, numbskull!

154
00:10:55,090 --> 00:10:57,900
Everyone's already left for the assembly!

155
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:00,310
Are you boycotting it or something?

156
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:02,060
Hurry!

157
00:11:02,060 --> 00:11:05,030
The closing assembly of our second year is about to start!

158
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:18,960
Issei...

159
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:21,030
How are things going on the mountain?

160
00:11:22,210 --> 00:11:25,460
The rebuilding of the main hall just got underway.

161
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:28,090
Everyone's working hard.

162
00:11:28,090 --> 00:11:32,090
Times such as these truly test a head priest's mettle.

163
00:11:32,090 --> 00:11:35,450
Admittedly, I'm barely even a novice...

164
00:11:35,450 --> 00:11:39,150
But it's enough to make me want to 
bow in gratitude to our parishioners.

165
00:11:39,150 --> 00:11:41,850
Yeah, I'll come by to help out soon.

166
00:11:41,850 --> 00:11:44,670
That reminds me, how is Shinji doing?

167
00:11:44,670 --> 00:11:47,110
He's been in the hospital for quite some time.

168
00:11:47,430 --> 00:11:48,990
Oh, don't worry.

169
00:11:48,990 --> 00:11:51,310
He should be discharged any day now.

170
00:11:51,310 --> 00:11:53,620
Sakura's been going to visit him daily.

171
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:58,450
Oh, his little sister is checking in on him every day, eh?

172
00:11:58,450 --> 00:12:01,920
Yeah, from what I can see, she's worn Shinji down.

173
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:03,370
Sakura's a tenacious girl,

174
00:12:03,970 --> 00:12:06,000
so he's been browbeaten into letting her look after him.

175
00:12:07,030 --> 00:12:09,010
That's wonderful news.

176
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:18,600
Just the two kids I was looking for!

177
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:27,050
It's been a month since anyone's heard from him,

178
00:12:27,050 --> 00:12:30,610
and we have a new teacher starting next semester.

179
00:12:31,150 --> 00:12:36,140
We'll look after Kuzuki-sensei's personal effects at the temple.

180
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:39,160
He turned up at the temple out of nowhere in the first place,

181
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:41,900
so I suppose it's fitting that he left us the same way.

182
00:12:50,550 --> 00:12:53,150
Well, if it isn't the student council president.

183
00:12:53,150 --> 00:12:55,430
Already up and patrolling the school?

184
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,430
Or are you doing maintenance on the club rooms?

185
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:01,310
Tohsaka!

186
00:13:01,310 --> 00:13:03,760
I tire of saying it so often,

187
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:06,440
but you really are diligent that way, aren't you?

188
00:13:07,310 --> 00:13:10,200
I've grown rather tired of our rote exchanges, myself!

189
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:12,920
Why not try guessing something new every once in a while?

190
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:16,820
I'm sure you haven't been deliberately 
repeating yourself, have you, Tohsaka?

191
00:13:16,820 --> 00:13:19,370
Of course I have.

192
00:13:19,370 --> 00:13:22,060
What? You never figured that out?

193
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:24,330
Ryuudou-kun sure is uptight,

194
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:27,470
don't you think?

195
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:30,750
Wh-What's the meaning of this, Emiya?!

196
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:34,380
What manner of relationship are you in with this foul vixen?!

197
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:35,220
Uh, I...

198
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:38,480
Anyway, come get me in my classroom later, Emiya-kun.

199
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:40,720
I'll wait until you get there.

200
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:42,650
Wh-What in the world?

201
00:13:42,650 --> 00:13:44,230
Oh!

202
00:13:44,630 --> 00:13:46,850
There you are, President!

203
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:49,770
Mitsuzuri Ayako...

204
00:13:49,770 --> 00:13:53,480
Would you mind explaining the new budget?

205
00:13:53,830 --> 00:13:56,750
Why does my club's funding have to be slashed?

206
00:13:56,750 --> 00:13:58,610
The archery club isn't the only one!

207
00:13:58,610 --> 00:14:02,210
All club budgets have had to be reviewed.

208
00:14:02,210 --> 00:14:04,120
I don't buy it!

209
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:07,550
You'll stand right there and explain yourself!

210
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:14,880
Say, Emiya-kun...

211
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:17,270
Were you ever in the track club?

212
00:14:17,270 --> 00:14:19,020
Track club?

213
00:14:19,020 --> 00:14:22,770
No, I was always in the archery club.

214
00:14:22,770 --> 00:14:24,230
Oh...

215
00:14:24,230 --> 00:14:27,480
Well, I guess these things happen.

216
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:29,900
I was just looking at the sunset, and it reminded me.

217
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:33,530
You have to admit, it's flown by in a flash.

218
00:14:33,530 --> 00:14:39,650
It's been a month since the Holy Grail War ended 
and you signed on as my pupil.

219
00:14:39,650 --> 00:14:42,530
At this rate, the next year will fly by.

220
00:14:42,530 --> 00:14:46,290
After that happens, we'll be leaving this school behind.

221
00:14:47,270 --> 00:14:50,040
What do you plan to do after graduation?

222
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:53,040
Follow in your father's footsteps?

223
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:56,110
Uh, yeah... Why?

224
00:14:56,110 --> 00:14:59,660
After I graduate, I'm going to London.

225
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:03,550
In light of everything that happened, 
the Mages' Association wrote me a letter of recommendation.

226
00:15:03,550 --> 00:15:07,540
London? The Mages' Association's headquarters?

227
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:09,060
That Clock Tower place?

228
00:15:09,530 --> 00:15:13,340
I've been invited as the Tohsaka family heir.

229
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:17,360
They say I can bring a pupil with me if I like.

230
00:15:18,020 --> 00:15:19,990
Um, does that mean...

231
00:15:21,990 --> 00:15:22,680
So.

232
00:15:24,150 --> 00:15:25,800
What will you be doing?

233
00:15:27,890 --> 00:15:32,090
Damn it. You always go right for my weak spot.

234
00:15:32,750 --> 00:15:33,800
What?

235
00:15:34,650 --> 00:15:35,750
Look...

236
00:15:35,750 --> 00:15:39,710
This is important, so give me a straight answer.

237
00:15:39,710 --> 00:15:42,510
Will you come with me?

238
00:15:45,790 --> 00:15:48,770
Don't ask when you already know the answer.

239
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:53,020
Then let's keep up the good work, Emiya-kun!

240
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:59,690
I'm gonna whip you into shape until 
you're a proper mage, so brace yourself!

241
00:15:59,690 --> 00:16:06,090
My life's goal is to make you into a new man—
one who's happy through and through.

242
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:19,800
Thanks for bringing me with you.

243
00:16:57,190 --> 00:16:58,000
Excuse me.

244
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:01,770
You are the exchange student from Japan?

245
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:04,880
Actually, that would be Tohsaka.

246
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:07,280
I know that.

247
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:10,220
I was referring to you.

248
00:17:10,220 --> 00:17:12,520
You're from Fuyuki City in Japan, right?

249
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:15,870
You don't seem to have the makings of a mage.

250
00:17:15,870 --> 00:17:22,280
I imagine you were an outsider who was caught up in the ritual and missed his chance to get out?

251
00:17:22,710 --> 00:17:24,620
I find it puzzling.

252
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:27,840
After surviving that troublesome war,

253
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:30,920
to what end have you come to Clock Tower?

254
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:33,290
To what end do you study magic?

255
00:17:34,850 --> 00:17:36,120
Good question.

256
00:17:36,790 --> 00:17:39,470
Since coming here, I've learned many things,

257
00:17:39,470 --> 00:17:42,050
and in many ways, I've been out of my depth.

258
00:17:42,810 --> 00:17:46,140
But I want to keep believing in what I believed in before.

259
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:49,580
I want to dedicate my life to that.

260
00:17:49,580 --> 00:17:51,310
Meaning what, exactly?

261
00:17:51,310 --> 00:17:55,310
Well, I realize how dumb this sounds...

262
00:17:56,310 --> 00:17:58,150
But I want to become something.

263
00:18:00,150 --> 00:18:02,320
A champion of justice.

264
00:18:06,450 --> 00:18:09,580
I see. That certainly is idiotic.

265
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:11,260
But it is nothing to laugh at.

266
00:18:12,250 --> 00:18:13,850
A champion of justice, hmm?

267
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:18,140
Yes, I suppose such a man would find this place stifling.

268
00:18:27,090 --> 00:18:28,540
Tohsaka?

269
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:30,970
Did we have plans for dinner?

270
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:34,470
I was waiting for you.

271
00:18:36,010 --> 00:18:38,730
Well? What did you do about enrollment?

272
00:18:39,930 --> 00:18:41,980
Oh, I turned them down.

273
00:18:43,980 --> 00:18:46,240
You're not angry?

274
00:18:46,990 --> 00:18:49,670
I knew this would happen.

275
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:53,730
Oh, but if you aren't going to join Clock Tower,

276
00:18:53,730 --> 00:18:57,000
I guess that means I'll be thrown out in three years too.

277
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:59,750
No, that doesn't mean you have to—

278
00:19:02,870 --> 00:19:04,750
Are you sure, though?

279
00:19:04,750 --> 00:19:07,380
I've been thinking about it nonstop,

280
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:10,790
but I don't think I'll ever be able to change how I live.

281
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:15,510
Even when I know I'm not right, I can't change paths.

282
00:19:18,890 --> 00:19:20,570
It's just as he said...

283
00:19:20,570 --> 00:19:22,750
I'll meet the same fate.

284
00:19:22,750 --> 00:19:25,450
He's right. I agree with him there.

285
00:19:25,450 --> 00:19:27,650
You're full of mistakes, Shirou.

286
00:19:27,980 --> 00:19:32,290
You're probably on the same path, 
heading in the same direction.

287
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:35,910
The difference might be in how far you can go.

288
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:42,150
What matters is where you end up, 
and how far you came, right?

289
00:19:42,150 --> 00:19:45,420
Even if your destination 
and the result end up being the same,

290
00:19:45,420 --> 00:19:48,480
if you manage to walk a little further afterward,

291
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:51,630
I know you'll get your proper ending.

292
00:19:52,430 --> 00:19:53,800
I see.

293
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:56,140
I really hope it turns out like that.

294
00:19:56,140 --> 00:20:00,340
No, I guess hoping isn't enough. 
I need to make sure that's what happens.

295
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:01,890
I wouldn't worry.

296
00:20:01,890 --> 00:20:05,650
I mean, you've had your answer all along.

297
00:20:06,070 --> 00:20:07,530
But are you really sure?

298
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:11,870
Clock Tower is an important place to you, right?

299
00:20:11,870 --> 00:20:13,530
I'll be fine.

300
00:20:13,530 --> 00:20:16,160
In the end, I'll probably settle down at Clock Tower.

301
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:19,430
But I want to look around and get things out of my system.

302
00:20:19,430 --> 00:20:21,540
You know, see the world.

303
00:20:21,540 --> 00:20:25,170
So now it's my turn to drag you around with me, huh?

304
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:28,640
Yeah, though that's all a ways off yet.

305
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:35,430
Regardless, having fun, suffering, seeing the sights,

306
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:38,810
and eventually having our own happily ever after...

307
00:20:41,530 --> 00:20:44,350
That's the future in store for us.

308
00:22:41,290 --> 00:22:42,870
A boy once said,

309
00:22:43,810 --> 00:22:45,930
"I don't want to watch people die."

310
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:52,190
"Shouldn't it be possible to save all who suffer?"

311
00:22:53,290 --> 00:22:56,950
What the boy was trying to cut down was himself.

312
00:22:57,930 --> 00:23:00,880
He wielded his sword for what he came to believe in.

313
00:23:02,310 --> 00:23:06,700
There is no longer a path where his battle ends and he turns back.

314
00:23:08,150 --> 00:23:11,050
However, he did get his answer.

315
00:23:11,050 --> 00:23:12,570
He has regrets.

316
00:23:12,570 --> 00:23:15,460
And he doesn't know how many times 
he has wished to do it all over.

317
00:23:16,530 --> 00:23:18,910
This fate is set in stone,

318
00:23:18,910 --> 00:23:21,090
and Emiya will probably go on cursing it.

319
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:23,220
But even still,

320
00:23:24,330 --> 00:23:27,680
I was not wrong.

